The overall T3 outcome rule in `refcheck/t3.py` is corrected to clarification 2: a non-comparable position can no longer leave a `pass`. The suite went from 514 tests to 519, all passing, and the work is in two commits, not pushed.

The protocol snapshot hash matched `76504d78…5e7c` before I started.

## Changes
**`refcheck/t3.py`** (`summarise`, which builds the overall, band and class summaries):
- **New outcome:** I added `incomplete`.
- **New field:** every summary now has `coverage_complete`. It is true only when the group has evaluated positions and none of them is non-comparable. This makes the incomplete coverage explicit next to a `fail`, as the clarification requires; before, you could only infer it from the counts.
- **Per-position reasons are kept:** `non_finite` (with NaN and ±inf counts for each array) and `ref64_above_binary32_range`.
- **One small change outside the outcome rule:** the `ULP32_DEFINITION` string in the output said "proposed, awaiting owner confirmation". That is no longer true, so it now states the confirmed definition and the FLT_MAX rule. Nothing it calculates changed.
- **Unchanged:** the reference numerics, the comparability gate, the refusal logic, the metrics and the f64 guard. I did not read or implement anything for the logit-dump specification.

**`tests/test_t3.py`:**
- Three assertions that encoded the old rule now expect `incomplete`: the non-finite test, the `early` band test and the native class.
- Five new tests:
  - every outcome, checked directly through `summarise`;
  - a violation alongside a non-comparable position gives `fail`;
  - representability at ±FLT_MAX and at the next binary64 value;
  - both branches of the ulp₃₂ definition at every power of two;
  - FLT_MAX equals (2 − 2⁻²³)·2¹²⁷ exactly.

## Outcome values (overall, and for every band and class)
| Value | When |
|---|---|
| `pass` | every evaluated position is comparable, and every logit satisfies T3 |
| `fail` | any comparable evaluated logit violates T3, even if other positions are non-comparable (then `coverage_complete` is false and those positions are listed) |
| `incomplete` | no comparable violation, but at least one evaluated position is non-comparable; not a pass |
| `empty_comparable_set` | no evaluated position is comparable; never a pass |
| `no_evaluated_positions` | bands and classes only, unchanged: no evaluated position falls in that band or class |

## Representability and ulp₃₂
- **Representability:** a position is non-comparable exactly when |ref₆₄| > FLT_MAX, compared on the binary64 value without converting it to binary32. It is checked after the non-finite check and before any part of the inequality. The code already did this.
  - ±FLT_MAX is in range and passes.
  - The next binary64 value, ±(FLT_MAX + 2⁷⁵), is non-comparable with reason `ref64_above_binary32_range`.
- **ulp₃₂** already matched clarification 1, so its calculation did not change. It computes 2^(max(e−1, −126) − 23), where e comes from `frexp`, which is exact. That gives 2⁻¹⁴⁹ for |x| < 2⁻¹²⁶ (±0 included) and 2^(⌊log₂|x|⌋ − 23) otherwise. It uses only ref₆₄ and never a platform logarithm.

## Test counts
- Before: 514 tests, OK.
- After: 519 tests, OK. The T3 test file went from 34 to 39.
- One of my new assertions failed on the first run: I had wrongly expected the `late` band to show incomplete coverage, but the non-comparable row is in the `early` band. I corrected the test, not the code.

