## New ambiguity: AMB-032
Clarification 2 lists "incomplete inputs" as one of the per-position reasons. But D12 says an incomplete triple must be refused before any verdict, and that is what the checker does: a missing row, a short array, a position outside the rows or a missing record refuses the whole evaluation. So an accepted triple can never have a position with incomplete inputs. I kept refusal at the triple level and changed nothing. Either reading avoids a false pass. The question for the owner is whether a future dump reader should report "incomplete" per position instead of refusing the whole dump.
